	(text "U4 boosts the switched battery to 5.06 V (set by R7/R8) for the\ncomputer and its screen, sized for 1.5 A. When U4 is off its output\nis disconnected from the battery.\nQ1, Q2, R9 and R10 make a one-way switch (an ideal diode): 5 V flows\nout to the computer, never back, so a Pi or P4 plugged into USB\ncan't charge the battery through U4.\nLayout: U4's switching loop (U4, C13, C14) stays small, on GND_PWR,\nat the far side of the block from U1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193.04 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "068c7bf1-3a18-4ae8-b418-301124f8503f")
	)
	(text "Dial"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 85.09 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "15aa80c8-564c-4117-b6e4-5b2d8cf5e667")
	)
	(text "Low-battery cutoff"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 233.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1a8048b3-7896-43b3-af3d-99f1c607b8d8")
	)
	(text "HUANO 4.5 mm mouse-wheel encoder, laid on its back\n(fitted by hand, left out of the PCBway BOM).\nC is the common pin. U7's pull-ups hold A and B high."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3c51b523-93b0-4248-8ee7-e7c497af41f3")
	)
	(text "Link to the computer"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4ba07a05-2edb-44e8-ac8b-1a5da0d5988c")
	)
	(text "Power"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 90.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "547b204a-56f9-4ab6-b255-0a8004be128b")
	)
	(text "J4 joins the Pi or P4 interposer with a straight 1x8 Dupont cable.\nThe order is fail-safe: reversed, 5V lands on 5V; shifted by one, on GND.\nGND_PWR carries the computer's and the boost's return current to J2\nthrough NT1, so it never crosses the audio ground.\nNo I2C pull-ups here: the Pi interposer and the P4 board bring their own."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "575416d5-95fe-4e96-a641-b0f87d42594d")
	)
	(text "Speaker"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 274.32 54.61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66723fa4-9916-4567-afd3-8cb7458380a7")
	)
	(text "U2 rebuilds the Pi's PWM audio from a quiet local 3.0 V (U3),\nso noise on the Pi's own supply and ground stays out of it.\nR3 + C1: 16 kHz low-pass. C10 is U3's output capacitor and\nU2's supply bypass; on the board it sits between them.\nR15 holds AUDIO low when nothing drives it (P4 builds\nplay through the P4 board's own speaker amp)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 167.64 151.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "79c26229-e3dd-44dd-a399-67ce43153174")
	)
	(text "J2  Maclock power harness (silk + -): pin 1 = battery +, about 3 to 4.2 V,\n    pin 2 = GND, 3-4 unused\nJ1  Maclock power switch, in series with the battery (closed = on)\nMolex PicoBlade 1.25 mm, 1 A per contact\nNT1 joins GND_PWR to the board ground at J2, the only place they meet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7b56a736-91a2-439e-b953-9fb9b8fe655a")
	)
	(text "Buttons"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "89a50fab-75bb-468c-b2fe-905b04cb7fc8")
	)
	(text "Input chip"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.72 85.09 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "974a4e52-4d22-437a-b25b-217f81b1da20")
	)
	(text "C2/R4 and C3/R5 feed the differential input; with the\nPAM8302A's internal 10k the gain is about 9 dB.\nR6 holds SD high from BOOST_EN: the amp is on whenever the\nboost is, and the low-battery cutoff shuts it down too.\nJ3 speaker: 8 ohm, 1 W, Molex PicoBlade plug;\npolarity does not matter."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 167.64 78.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bec27d6d-abe0-461c-96bf-06a62cb9edff")
	)
	(text "U7 reads the dial and both buttons (I2C address 0x20) through its own\n100 kOhm pull-ups and pulls INT low when one changes. VDD comes from the\nswitched battery: its I2C input-high threshold, 0.7 x VDD, stays under\nthe 3.3 V bus. P4-P7 are unused; their pull-ups hold them high."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.72 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c6a00aa3-ca51-4210-88d9-70ae93264c82")
	)
	(text "Battery gauge"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.72 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d04973be-4dfd-4692-9911-5256802882fc")
	)
	(text "Audio amplifier"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 167.64 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d11c93ba-3aba-4733-9dcd-14ae731b4ace")
	)
	(text "U6 reports the battery's charge in percent over I2C (address 0x36).\nIt runs from the switched battery, as on the P4 interposer: with the\ncomputer off its I2C lines sit low, and the datasheet says the gauge\nmay then stop tracking. Its CELL pin senses at J1. ALRT is unused."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.72 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d643c754-e209-4f4f-a196-987dc123b8e6")
	)
	(text "U7's pull-ups hold BTN1/BTN2 high; R1/R2 limit\ncurrent into its pins.\nSW pins 3-4 are the metal bracket."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e68daee9-a17d-461e-b38c-deb351929203")
	)
	(text "U5 pulls LOWBAT_N low while the battery is under 3.08 V. Through R12 that\npulls BOOST_EN down against R13+R17, slowed by C16 and C19 (about 3 s).\nWhen the PNP half of Q3 gets about 0.6 V it fires, Q3 latches, and\nBOOST_EN stays low until the power switch is turned off. That stops U4,\nwhich would otherwise run the cell down to 0.5 V, and the amp (R6), which\nwould draw about 4 mA. A battery at 3.0 V latches after about 2.5 s.\nPower-up can't trip it: U5's start-up reset lasts at most 560 ms, in which\nthe PNP sees at most about 0.3 V. Dips shorter than about 2 s are ignored.\nC20 keeps noise from firing the latch; D1 stops BOOST_EN going below ground\nas C16/C19 discharge when the switch is turned off. About 0.15 mA in all\nwhile latched off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e747cb93-ab14-4f79-b2f4-3285f605a207")
	)
	(text "5 V boost and one-way switch"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 167.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e9c4c2aa-0903-4522-97a7-89deb2b5f9c6")
	)
